 "text": "Hello, how are things going? It depends on the kind of paint. Go light with thin layers, and wait until the oil is dry to the touch, not just on the surface. You close. Oil takes about six weeks from the day you stop building it, so you' want to stop a week early. Yes, you can use a spray on quick drying varnish. One coat takes about a day, and you can touch it after an hour. Gently rub a clean cloth with your thumb. If it leaves mark, it needs another coat.",
